From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Novikov <dj.novikov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0300
Subject: net: bridge: mrp: run the ring in software on plain NICs

With CONFIG_NET_SWITCHDEV=y the bridge asks the switchdev drivers for
the MRP instance and the ring role and refuses the ring when nobody
answers: "mrp addmrp" fails with -EOPNOTSUPP on a bridge of ordinary
NICs, although such a bridge forwards every frame in software and the
software MRP needs nothing from the hardware.  Without NET_SWITCHDEV
the same bridge runs MRP in software.

Accept -EOPNOTSUPP for the MRP instance, and for the ring role when no
ring port is offloaded by a switchdev driver (offload_count 0).  An
offloaded port still has to accept the role with sw_backup, which
promises that MRP frames reach the CPU.

Tested on NanoPi R6S (RTL8125, RK3588S) as MRC in a ring with
NAPI-Switch (MRM): ring break and closure, 128-145 ms recovery.
---
--- a/net/bridge/br_mrp.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_mrp.c
@@ -535,8 +535,11 @@
 	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&mrp->in_test_work, br_mrp_in_test_work_expired);
 	hlist_add_tail_rcu(&mrp->list, &br->mrp_list);
 
+	/* No switchdev driver takes the MRP instance: -EOPNOTSUPP. The
+	 * instance then runs in software, as the ring role and test do.
+	 */
 	err = br_mrp_switchdev_add(br, mrp);
-	if (err)
+	if (err && err != -EOPNOTSUPP)
 		goto delete_mrp;
 
 	return 0;
--- a/net/bridge/br_mrp_switchdev.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_mrp_switchdev.c
@@ -61,6 +61,21 @@
 	return switchdev_port_obj_del(br->dev, &mrp_obj.obj);
 }
 
+/* No ring port is offloaded by a switchdev driver: the bridge forwards
+ * every frame in software, nothing has to trap MRP frames to the CPU.
+ */
+static bool br_mrp_ring_in_software(struct br_mrp *mrp)
+{
+#ifdef CONFIG_NET_SWITCHDEV
+	struct net_bridge_port *p = rtnl_dereference(mrp->p_port);
+	struct net_bridge_port *s = rtnl_dereference(mrp->s_port);
+
+	return !(p && p->offload_count) && !(s && s->offload_count);
+#else
+	return true;
+#endif
+}
+
 enum br_mrp_hw_support
 br_mrp_switchdev_set_ring_role(struct net_bridge *br, struct br_mrp *mrp,
 			       enum br_mrp_ring_role_type role)
@@ -95,6 +110,10 @@
 	if (!err)
 		return BR_MRP_SW;
 
+	/* Plain NICs: no driver answers, run the ring in software. */
+	if (err == -EOPNOTSUPP && br_mrp_ring_in_software(mrp))
+		return BR_MRP_SW;
+
 	return BR_MRP_NONE;
 }
 
